WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.050
I am Rajan Kumar V K. I have taught for more than ten years, first in school science laboratories in Nepal, and then at LUT University in Finland.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.020
My teaching rests on four principles.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:19.810
The first is clarity. A complex idea should be made simple, without losing its meaning.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:30.340
The second is relevance. Students learn best when they see why knowledge matters, so I bring real industrial problems, and my own research, into the classroom.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:37.000
The third is a student-centred environment, where people feel safe to ask, to doubt, and to try.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.950
The fourth is the one closest to me.

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:42.530
Learning is insight, not accumulation.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:47.760
Fear suppresses curiosity. Freedom to question is where understanding begins.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:51.090
So my role is to guide, not to dominate.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:52.510
I ask before I tell.

